<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/055A">Remark <span data-tag="055A">3.5.7.23</span>.</a> Let $f: X \rightarrow Y$ and be a morphism of Kan complexes, and let $g: Y \rightarrow Z$ be a homotopy equivalence of Kan complexes. Then $f$ exhibits $Y$ as an $n$-truncation of $X$ if and only if $g \circ f$ exhibits $Z$ as an $n$-truncation of $X$. See Corollaries <a data-tag="04H9" href="/tag/04H9">3.5.1.28</a> and <a data-tag="0550" href="/tag/0550">3.5.7.8</a>. </p>
